From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Test the DateTime::Locale 1.35 C alias explicitly

DateTime::Locale 1.35 canonicalizes the C locale as en-US, whereas the
older 1.00-1.34 range used en-US-POSIX. The upstream test assumes every
version at least 1.00 returns the older identifier, so its locale
assertion fails on the fixed openEuler SP3 provider even though all
DateTime conversion fields and the timezone pass. Keep assertion 11 and
its concrete expected value; add the 1.35 branch without skipping or
reducing any of the 15 assertions in this file.

---
 t/02_main.t | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/t/02_main.t b/t/02_main.t
--- a/t/02_main.t
+++ b/t/02_main.t
@@ -65,2 +65,3 @@
-	# DateTime::Locale version 1.00 changes "C" to "en-US-POSIX".
-	my $expected = eval { DateTime::Locale->VERSION(1) } ? "en-US-POSIX" : "C";
+	# DateTime::Locale 1.35 changes "C" from "en-US-POSIX" to "en-US".
+	my $expected = eval { DateTime::Locale->VERSION(1.35) } ? "en-US"
+	             : eval { DateTime::Locale->VERSION(1) } ? "en-US-POSIX" : "C";
